  "body": "**Stacked on #798** (Tormach microARC 4, issue #785). This branch merges #798's head (`f99f045e`). Until #798 merges, this PR's diff also shows #798's files. Review only the files listed under \"What changed\". Merge #798 first, then re-check this PR with `git merge origin/main`.\n\nFork synced at v0.16.0 (process files PROCESS_VERSION 10). Upstream main is merged into this branch because the code it fixes landed after v0.16.0 (#785). Correction: #785's code has not landed on upstream main. It is still open as #798, which is why this PR is stacked on it.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe machine check judged a tilted move's canonical letters one by one. On the 770MX + microARC 4, whose only rotary is an A about X, it refused the face underneath (A0 B180) with \"states no B axis\". That table reaches the pose as A180, and the PathPilot post already posts it as `G0 A180`.\n\n- `crates/app/src/machine/judge.rs`: the pose gate moves here from `mod.rs` as `pose_problems`.\n  - On a machine with exactly one rotary, stated along X (the post's own test, x² ≥ 0.998·|d|²), the gate reads the tool angle about X from the letters. It uses the post's formula and tolerances (`tormach.cps` `toolAngle`), so the check and the post agree on every pose.\n  - The angle is signed by the stated direction (a `[-1,0,0]` table commands the negated angle, as the post writes the word) and judged against the rotary's travel.\n  - A pose with an X component, meaning any B or C a turn about X cannot make, is refused by name: `move i commands A .. B .. C .. deg; <model>'s only rotary, A about X, cannot reach that pose`.\n  - Every other machine keeps the letter law unchanged: none, two or more rotaries, or a single rotary that is unstated or not along X.\n- `crates/app/src/machine/mod.rs`: calls `pose_problems` instead of the inline letter loop. The file shrinks from 396 to 355 lines.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`: this post writes the stream's letters as they come (G43.4), so it now refuses a turning letter with no rotary of that name: `tilted move commands B - the machine states no B rotary`. Before this PR, the check stopped A0 B180 reaching that dialect on an A-only table. Now the post does, so the safety floor is unchanged.\n- `crates/app/tests/microarc_test_part.rs` (from #798): the wrap test now expects the post's refusal (`simultaneous 4-axis motion in operation WRAP`). It also asserts that the machine check no longer flags the wrap, whose every pose is reachable as an angle about X. The header comment is updated.\n- `docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/README.md`: one sentence updated to match.\n- `docs/decisions/797-a-only-pose.md`: the decision record.\n\n## How tested\n\nThe new suite, `crates/app/tests/fourth_axis_pose.rs`, holds the pinning tests:\n\n- `an_a0_b180_slot_posts_as_a180_on_the_microarc4`: a real Slot with tilt A0 B180 on the bar job, built through the app's commands.\n  - The check is clean.\n  - `post_setup` writes exactly one index, `G0 A180`, and no B word.\n  - The cuts land on the skin (Z 0.375 → 0.36) inside the stick-out.\n- `the_face_underneath_is_judged_as_a180_against_the_travel`:\n  - With A travel -90..90, every move is refused as `commands A 180.000 deg (the pose A 0.000 B 180.000), the travel is -90.000..90.000`.\n  - A `[-1,0,0]` table commands -180: it passes on -180..0 and is refused on 0..180.\n- `a_pose_the_a_axis_cannot_reach_is_still_refused_by_name`: a B30 lean on the same machine is refused by name by the check, and `post_setup` refuses and writes no file.\n- `a_second_rotary_keeps_the_letter_law`: A about X plus C about Z still refuses B180 with `states no B axis`.\n- `the_fanuc_dialect_refuses_a_b_on_an_a_only_table`: fanuc.cps on the microARC mirror refuses A0 B180 by name and writes no `B180`. A90 posts.\n\nGate: the plan from `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`. It falls to every app suite because #798's golden is shared test input. It was run with `-j 2` (the xtask hard-codes `-j 6`, which exhausts the Windows paging file here). Results per step:\n\n- post suites (`camcraft-post --lib`): 7 passed.\n- app suites (the lib plus 234 test binaries, `fourth_axis_pose` among them): 1775 passed, 1 failed. The one failure is `microarc_test_part::the_microarc_test_part_posts_its_indexed_program`. It comes from #798 and is a Windows checkout issue:\n  - The kit golden `docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/microarc_test_part.nc` is not covered by the `eol=lf` rule in `.gitattributes`, so an `autocrlf` checkout gives it CRLF line endings.\n  - The posted program matches the golden apart from line endings. With the file converted to LF, the binary passes 2/2.\n  - The fix (a `.gitattributes` line) belongs in #798, so it is not made here.\n- ui suite (`camcraft-ui --test machine`, CWD `crates/ui`): 6 passed.\n- Other touched binaries, also run alone: `machine` 33/33, `fanuc_post` 11/11, `tormach_fourth_axis` 10/10, `fourth_axis_pose` 5/5.\n\n`cargo clippy -j 2 -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean (exit 0).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real PathPilot or Fanuc control was run.\n- The release-lane `--ignored` heavy tests were not run.\n- The ui snapshot lane was not run.\n- The kit golden CRLF failure above (from #798) is not fixed here.\n\nChangelog: The machine check reads a 4th-axis A-about-X table's pose through the tool axis, so the face underneath (A0 B180) posts as A180 on the 770MX + microARC 4; an unreachable pose is still refused by name, and the Fanuc post refuses a letter the machine has no rotary for.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #797\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
